      "content": "thanks man, i really needed to hear that. i was looking at the logs from the staging stress test again just now and i saw some weird latency spikes in the ledger update timing—nothing crazy, but it looked a little jittery during the peak bursts. i'm assuming that's just the staging environment being slow and not anything to do with how we're handling the locks, right? just double check that specific timing loop one more time so i don't look like an idiot when i tell the VP we're 100% clear.",
